Narrator: She turns and walks back into town, and does not come looking for him again.
Narrator: Catherine's last days pass quietly, among the people and creatures she's come to know in Shateroo.
Narrator: She dies young  but without bitterness, surrounded by more warmth than she expected to find at the edge of the world.
Narrator: Marloch had braced for hatred, the way he'd always been hated.
Narrator: Instead, he watches humans and monsters mourn her together, side by side, and something old and closed in him creaks open, just slightly.
Narrator: He begins granting wishes again. But only to those he judges worthy of one.
